WEBVTT

00:00:00.315 --> 00:00:01.054
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:04.553
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Here’s a solid gold piece of advice:

00:00:05.143 --> 00:00:09.090
be wary of anyone offering you solid gold pieces of advice.

00:00:10.991 --> 00:00:11.712
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:12.521 --> 00:00:15.065
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The friend who advises you to, say,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:19.530
stay in your relationship or leave your job may well be looking out for you,

00:00:19.549 --> 00:00:22.872
but she’s inescapably looking out for herself, too.

00:00:23.788 --> 00:00:24.568
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:25.495 --> 00:00:28.466
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> People will generally advise you to act more cautiously

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:31.373
than they would act themselves in a similar situation

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:34.335
– perhaps because they don’t want it on their conscience

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.482
if you take a daring leap and fall flat on your face.

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.068
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:45.189
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> There’s a happy flip side to this, though, for parents, teachers, managers,

00:00:45.497 --> 00:00:49.483
and anyone else who finds themselves in the position of needing to motivate others.

00:00:51.294 --> 00:00:52.103
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:55.544
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> This result isn’t all that surprising, I suppose,

00:00:55.569 --> 00:00:59.596
when you consider how flattering it feels to be invited to give advice.

00:01:01.537 --> 00:01:02.405
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:01:03.301 --> 00:01:07.871
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Yet the truth, very often, is that we know exactly what we need to do

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:10.246
– we just lack the confidence to do it.

00:01:12.168 --> 00:01:12.942
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:15.997
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> To ingratiate yourself with someone,

00:01:16.145 --> 00:01:19.458
it’s better to ask for a favour than to perform one:

00:01:20.039 --> 00:01:23.049
the favour-doer will come to think of you as the decent

00:01:23.074 --> 00:01:26.045
and likeable sort for whom they do favours.